ake a day off they're  gonna play three days and take it off  and they're going to continue that the  time controls if you're looking at the  rules they start with a hundred minutes  that's going to be for the first 40  moves as soon as they cross the 40 move  mark they're gonna get in additional  fifty minutes for the next 20 moves and  then they'll have 15 minutes for the  rest of the game they will be adding on  30 seconds per move but that is the the  time control that we have going on in  the game there are some tie breakers if  we get to that point  I'll I'll make sure I mention those in  the video but my guess is we won't end  up in the tiebreaker we'll see them but  yeah March 17th make sure you mark your  calendars definitely expected everyone  to be watching all of the videos there's  not too many other things that you  should be watching at this time I'm  expecting a very very good tournament  these players if you've listened to the  interviews and if followed them they've  been preparing quite a bit so excited to  see how this ends up thank you guys so  much for watching the prep video  hopefully you're as excited as I am and  I'll see you guys in a couple days for  round one

